                "H₂S ⇌ H⁺ + HS⁻",
                "1.0 x 10⁻⁷",
                "Week"
              ],
              [
                "NH₄¹",
                "NH₄ ⇌ H⁺ + NH₅",
                "5.7 x 10⁻¹⁰",
                "Week"
              ],
              [
                "HCO₃⁻",
                "HCO₃ ⇌ H⁺ + CO₃²",
                "4.7 x 10⁻¹²",
                "Week"
              ],
              [
                "H₂O",
                "H₂O ⇌ H⁺ + OH⁻",
                "1.8 x 10⁻¹⁵",
                "Very week"
              ]
            ],
            "book_errors": [
              "(10⁻²)",
              "(10⁻⁵)",
              "1.3 x 10⁻⁴",
              "6.7 x 10⁻⁵",
              "H₂CO₃ ⇌ H⁺ + HS⁻",
              "NH₄¹",
              "NH₅",
              "+ CO₃²",
              "4.7 x 10⁻¹²",
              "1.8 x 10⁻¹⁵"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Book correction",
            "text": "Table 9.3 has several misprints. Strong acids have Ka much greater than 1, so the bracketed values cannot be right; approximate accepted values are HCl about 10⁶ to 10⁷, HNO₃ about 20 to 25 and H₂SO₄ (first step) about 10³. HSO₄⁻ has Ka about 1.2 × 10⁻², HF about 6.8 × 10⁻⁴ and HCO₃⁻ 4.7 × 10⁻¹¹. H₂CO₃ gives H⁺ + HCO₃⁻ (not HS⁻), the ammonium ion is NH₄⁺ (NH₄⁺ ⇌ H⁺ + NH₃), carbonate is CO₃²⁻, and water has Ka = 1.8 × 10⁻¹⁶ (Kw / 55.5, as in 9.3). “Week” is weak."
          }
        ]
      }
